From 6b5c776f7d183947847c677644c2e3465a18eff8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yiyu Zhou <yiyu@yiyuzhou.io>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 02:42:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/47] iris: accept the module arguments of nix-darwin

The module of iris is a function of an empty attribute set without an
ellipsis, but the module system calls every module with config, lib,
pkgs, and the other module arguments.  The call fails, so
darwinConfigurations.iris does not evaluate.  Take the arguments with
an ellipsis, as lexi does.
---
 machines/darwin/iris.nix | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/machines/darwin/iris.nix b/machines/darwin/iris.nix
index 6452831..df64c2c 100644
--- a/machines/darwin/iris.nix
+++ b/machines/darwin/iris.nix
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-{ }:
+{ ... }:
 {
   imports = [
     ./state-version.nix
-- 
2.56.1

